= Anthropomorphism — Simple =

'''Anthropomorphism''' is treating a nonhuman thing as if it has humanlike traits or a humanlike mind.

People might say a dog is jealous, a storm is angry, or a robot wants attention.

Sometimes an anthropomorphic description is wrong.

But it is not automatically wrong. Some animals really do have emotions, goals, memory, and social abilities that overlap with human abilities.

The important question is whether the specific claim has evidence.

Anthropomorphism is common with interactive technology because humanlike language and behavior make it easy to imagine a mind behind the system.

